{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_m56ngpcoa724in6h7cc67p4mdzbrqtcxkngddjjafufcjjh2jsra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The full C library in `c_src/` is translated to Rust, and both the ABI and the observable behavior are verified against the C build.\n\n## What was translated\nThe CMake build compiles exactly three sources into `libdriver.so`; all three are covered:\n\n| C file | Rust file | Functions |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/matrix.c` | `src/matrix.rs` | `allocate_matrix`, `free_matrix`, `initialize_matrix_from_string`, `multiply_matrices`, `matrix_to_string` |\n| `src/write.c` | `src/write.rs` | `write_to_file` |\n| `src/driver.c` | `src/driver.rs` | `driver` |\n| — | `src/cffi.rs` | libc bindings (`malloc`/`free`/`strdup`/`strtok_r`/`atoi`/`stdio`/`errno`), no external crates |\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n`nm -D --defined-only` on both `.so` files yields the identical 7-symbol set (`allocate_matrix`, `driver`, `free_matrix`, `initialize_matrix_from_string`, `matrix_to_string`, `multiply_matrices`, `write_to_file`); `comm -23 c_syms rust_syms` produced no output. No namespace-renaming macros exist in the headers, so source names are the final linker names.\n\n## Fidelity decisions\n- **Same allocator/stdio as C**: objects handed back to callers are `malloc`'d (so a caller's `free()`/`free_matrix()` is valid), and all diagnostics go through libc `perror`/`fprintf(stderr, …)` so message text, `strerror(errno)` values, and stream buffering/ordering match exactly.\n- **`matrix_t` is `#[repr(C)]`** — verified 16 bytes, same field offsets.\n- **C integer semantics preserved**: `int → size_t` sign-extension in `malloc(height * sizeof(int*))`, wrapping `int` arithmetic in the multiply accumulator and in `buffer_size` (so overflow → negative → huge `malloc` → `perror` path is reproduced).\n- **Bugs deliberately kept**: missing `NULL` check on `allocate_matrix` results; the `free(mat->matrix[j])` loop running `j <= i` over the just-failed `NULL` row; `free(res)` instead of `free_matrix(res)` in `driver`'s `res_str == NULL` branch (row leak); `strcat`-based string building with the original undersized buffer formula.\n\n## Verification performed\n- `cargo build --release` after `cargo clean`: compiles with zero warnings/errors.\n- A `dlopen`-based differential harness ran **30 scenarios** (valid/degenerate/zero/negative dimensions, malformed and short input strings, `atoi` quirks like `007`/`+9`/`abc`/`2147483648`, multiply overflow, dimension mismatch, `NULL` matrix/content, bad paths, directory target, and all `driver` paths) plus **6 extra edge cases**, comparing stdout, stderr, return codes, and the contents of `matrix.txt`/`out.txt` byte-for-byte between the C and Rust libraries. All 36 matched with no differences.\n- `c_src/` is unmodified (no files newer than the build)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":49563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1054,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cbf64a6-a9ab-4ea7-9861-97f53a95d92f","uuid":"f3fe1c97-6b23-43d6-9a69-d44afef6e186","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:33:51.300Z"}
